# promise: #483
# The sidebar out over a page, docked with the sidebar button: it grows into its docked place in its
# own panel on the window's slide, squaring its corners as its shadow fades, and the window takes it
# back once it is there. Swapped into the window first, it lost its corners, shadow and backdrop in
# one frame and jumped by the floating margin. The page stays where it ends up, as for ⌘S (#317).
budget rss=700 stalls50=10
cra://debug?windowSize=1280x800
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=dock
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
wait 1
cra://action/toggleSidebar
wait 1
cra://debug?floatingSidebar=1
wait 1
cra://debug?windowState=out
expect-log window state out: main0 .* sidebar=left edge=floating .* floating=left 5
cra://action/toggleSidebar
wait 1
expect-log sidebar docked in place: page moved 0 pt$
cra://debug?windowState=docked
expect-log window state docked: main0 .* lightsHidden=0 .* sidebar=left edge=left .* floating=none
